## 1. Verified KPI Targets

Goal: Accelerate supplier payment processing while minimizing delays in invoice handling and optimizing purchasing agent workload without overloading them.

  1. Average Cycle Time from Requisition to Invoice Payment [time] — minimize (scope: end_to_end)
  2. Average Wait Time Before Invoice Release [time] — minimize (scope: end_to_end)
  3. Purchasing Agent Workload Utilization [utilization] — minimize (scope: end_to_end)

Reasoning: This KPI set effectively addresses the simulation goal by focusing on the entire procurement process cycle time, the delay before invoice release, and the workload of purchasing agents. The first KPI captures the full cycle from requisition to payment, ensuring a comprehensive view of supplier payment efficiency. The second KPI targets the specific delay before invoice release, aligning with the need to minimize unnecessary delays. The third KPI measures the utilization of purchasing agents, ensuring that their workload is optimized without overloading them. All KPIs are grounded in the provided event log evidence and are measurable within the defined process context.

